{
  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent under-forecast bias in rising markets: model levels are ~5–12 EUR below realized prices across most of the 30-day horizon when a rally starts.",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the model captures direction but reacts too slowly to upward momentum; apply an upward drift adjustment when the last 5–10 days show a clear upswing.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: underestimation grows with lead time (small at days 1–3, larger by days 7–20+). Use a ramping correction factor that increases with horizon during uptrends.",
    "Over-mean-reversion: forecasts revert toward ~69–72 even as the market trends to ~80–84. Reduce mean-reversion strength (or increase trend weight) when price breaks above the recent 30-day range.",
    "Post-breakout regime shift not recognized: after a volatility expansion/upward breakout, the model continues forecasting within the prior regime band. Add a regime-switch uplift when price closes above prior 20–30d highs for multiple sessions."
  ]
}
